-- ccc21-part-18-1.l4 -- PART XVIII.1, Case Management Judge, ss 551.1 to 551.7 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core and this part's nouns (the mode of trial).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words: each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...): "<quote>"`); NOTHING (not covered: `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. `-- GRANT-GATE: ...` marks the groups NOTES.md counts for a lawyer. This Part names its parties by office (the Chief Justice or Chief Judge, the officer
-- who has custody of the indictment) and states no number of days, so it has no regulative rule: the duties are decision functions (NOTES.md "What the stable binary does not accept" and the seams).

§ `PART XVIII.1 -- Case Management Judge`

§§ `Section 551.1 -- Appointment`

-- 551.1 (1) On application by the prosecutor or the accused or on his or her own motion, the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge of the court before which a trial is to be or is being held or the judge that the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge designates may,
-- if he or she is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice, appoint a judge as the case management judge for that trial at any time before the jury selection, if the trial is before a judge and jury,
-- or before the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented, if the trial is being heard by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge.
-- src:12137 | 551.1 (1) On application by the prosecutor or the accused or on his or her own motion, the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge of the court before which a trial is to be or is being held or the judge that the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge designates may, if he or she is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice, appoint a judge as the case management judge for that trial at any time before the jury selection, if the trial is before a judge and jury, or before the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented, if the trial is being heard by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge.
@ref s 551.1(1) (src:12137-12137)
GIVEN `a trial is to be or is being held before the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge, or the judge designated, is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mode of trial` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial`
      `jury selection has begun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551.1(1) the Chief Justice or Chief Judge may appoint a judge as the case management judge for the trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a trial is to be or is being held before the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court before which a trial is to be or is being held"
        IF NOT `the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge, or the judge designated, is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he or she is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice"
        IF `the mode of trial` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` AND `jury selection has begun` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the jury selection, if the trial is before a judge and jury"
        IF (NOT (`the mode of trial` EQUALS `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`)) AND `the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented has been reached` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented, if the trial is being heard by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 551.1 (2) The Chief Justice or the Chief Judge or his or her designate may order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused or a hearing be held for the purpose of deciding
-- if it is necessary for the proper administration of justice to proceed with the appointment.
