§§ `Section 551.2 -- Role`

-- 551.2 The case management judge shall assist in promoting a fair and efficient trial, including by ensuring that the evidence on the merits is presented, to the extent possible, without interruption.
-- src:12144 | 551.2 The case management judge shall assist in promoting a fair and efficient trial, including by ensuring that the evidence on the merits is presented, to the extent possible, without interruption.
@ref s 551.2 (src:12144-12144)
GIVEN `the judge is the case management judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551.2 the case management judge shall assist in promoting a fair and efficient trial` MEANS
    IF `the judge is the case management judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The case management judge"

§§ `Section 551.3 -- Powers before evidence on merits presented`

-- 551.3 (1) In performing their duties before the stage of the presentation of the evidence on the merits, the case management judge, as a trial judge, exercises the powers that a trial judge has before that stage in order to assist
-- in promoting a fair and efficient trial, including by (a) ... (h): the powers the paragraphs list.
-- src:12146 | 551.3 (1) In performing their duties before the stage of the presentation of the evidence on the merits, the case management judge, as a trial judge, exercises the powers that a trial judge has before that stage in order to assist in promoting a fair and efficient trial, including by
-- src:12147 | (a) assisting the parties to identify the witnesses to be heard, taking into account the witnesses’ needs and circumstances;
-- src:12148 | (b) encouraging the parties to make admissions and reach agreements;
-- src:12149 | (c) encouraging the parties to consider any other matters that would promote a fair and efficient trial;
-- src:12150 | (d) establishing schedules and imposing deadlines on the parties;
-- src:12151 | (e) hearing guilty pleas and imposing sentences;
-- src:12152 | (f) assisting the parties to identify the issues that are to be dealt with at the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented;
-- src:12153 | (g) subject to section 551.7, adjudicating any issues that can be decided before that stage, including those related to
-- src:12154 | (i) the disclosure of evidence,
-- src:12155 | (ii) the admissibility of evidence,
-- src:12156 | (iii) the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms,
-- src:12157 | (iv) expert witnesses,
-- src:12158 | (v) the severance of counts, and
-- src:12159 | (vi) the separation of trials on one or more counts when there is more than one accused; and
-- src:12160 | (h) ordering, in each case set out in subsection 599(1), that the trial be held in a territorial division in the same province other than that in which the offence would otherwise be tried.
@ref s 551.3(1) (src:12146-12160)
DECLARE `s 551.3(1) the power` IS ONE OF
    `s 551.3(1)(a) assisting the parties to identify the witnesses to be heard, taking into account the witnesses’ needs and circumstances`
    `s 551.3(1)(b) encouraging the parties to make admissions and reach agreements`
    `s 551.3(1)(c) encouraging the parties to consider any other matters that would promote a fair and efficient trial`
    `s 551.3(1)(d) establishing schedules and imposing deadlines on the parties`
    `s 551.3(1)(e) hearing guilty pleas and imposing sentences`
    `s 551.3(1)(f) assisting the parties to identify the issues that are to be dealt with at the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented`
    `s 551.3(1)(g)(i) adjudicating an issue related to the disclosure of evidence`
    `s 551.3(1)(g)(ii) adjudicating an issue related to the admissibility of evidence`
    `s 551.3(1)(g)(iii) adjudicating an issue related to the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms`
    `s 551.3(1)(g)(iv) adjudicating an issue related to expert witnesses`
    `s 551.3(1)(g)(v) adjudicating an issue related to the severance of counts`
    `s 551.3(1)(g)(vi) adjudicating an issue related to the separation of trials on one or more counts when there is more than one accused`
    `s 551.3(1)(h) ordering, in a case set out in subsection 599(1), that the trial be held in a territorial division in the same province other than that in which the offence would otherwise be tried`
    `s 551.3(1) any other power a trial judge has before that stage`

