§§ `Section 551.7 -- Decision whether to hold joint hearing`

-- 551.7 (1) If an issue referred to in any of subparagraphs 551.3(1)(g)(i) to (iii) is to be adjudicated in related trials that are to be or are being held in the same province before a court of the same jurisdiction, the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge of that court
-- or his or her designate may, on application by the prosecutor or the accused or on his or her own motion, determine if it is in the interests of justice, including ensuring consistent decisions, to adjudicate that issue at a joint hearing for some or all of those trials.
-- src:12183 | 551.7 (1) If an issue referred to in any of subparagraphs 551.3(1)(g)(i) to (iii) is to be adjudicated in related trials that are to be or are being held in the same province before a court of the same jurisdiction, the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge of that court or his or her designate may, on application by the prosecutor or the accused or on his or her own motion, determine if it is in the interests of justice, including ensuring consistent decisions, to adjudicate that issue at a joint hearing for some or all of those trials.
@ref s 551.7(1) (src:12183-12183)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `s 551.3(1) the power`
      `the issue is to be adjudicated in related trials` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the related trials are to be or are being held in the same province before a court of the same jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551.7(1) the Chief Justice or Chief Judge may determine if it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the power` EQUALS `s 551.3(1)(g)(i) adjudicating an issue related to the disclosure of evidence` OR `the power` EQUALS `s 551.3(1)(g)(ii) adjudicating an issue related to the admissibility of evidence` OR `the power` EQUALS `s 551.3(1)(g)(iii) adjudicating an issue related to the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms`) THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an issue referred to in any of subparagraphs 551.3(1)(g)(i) to (iii)"
        IF NOT `the issue is to be adjudicated in related trials` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is to be adjudicated in related trials"
        IF NOT `the related trials are to be or are being held in the same province before a court of the same jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the same province before a court of the same jurisdiction"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 551.7 (2) To make the determination, the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge or his or her designate (a) shall take into account, among other considerations, the degree to which the evidence relating to the issue is similar in the related trials;
