-- 551.7 (3) If the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge or his or her designate determines that it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing for some or all of the related trials, he or she shall issue an order
-- (a) declaring that a joint hearing be held ...; (b) naming the parties who are to appear at the hearing; (c) appointing a judge to adjudicate the issue; and (d) designating the territorial division in which the hearing is to be held, if the trials are being held in different territorial divisions.
-- src:12189 | (3) If the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge or his or her designate determines that it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing for some or all of the related trials, he or she shall issue an order
-- src:12190 | (a) declaring that a joint hearing be held to adjudicate the issue in the related trials that he or she specifies;
-- src:12191 | (b) naming the parties who are to appear at the hearing;
-- src:12192 | (c) appointing a judge to adjudicate the issue; and
-- src:12193 | (d) designating the territorial division in which the hearing is to be held, if the trials are being held in different territorial divisions.
@ref s 551.7(3) (src:12189-12193)
DECLARE `s 551.7(3) the content of the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 551.7(3)(a) declaring that a joint hearing be held to adjudicate the issue in the related trials that are specified`
    `s 551.7(3)(b) naming the parties who are to appear at the hearing`
    `s 551.7(3)(c) appointing a judge to adjudicate the issue`
    `s 551.7(3)(d) designating the territorial division in which the hearing is to be held`
    `s 551.7(3) anything else`

-- src:12189 | (3) If the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge or his or her designate determines that it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing for some or all of the related trials, he or she shall issue an order
-- src:12190 | (a) declaring that a joint hearing be held to adjudicate the issue in the related trials that he or she specifies;
-- src:12191 | (b) naming the parties who are to appear at the hearing;
-- src:12192 | (c) appointing a judge to adjudicate the issue; and
-- src:12193 | (d) designating the territorial division in which the hearing is to be held, if the trials are being held in different territorial divisions.
@ref s 551.7(3) (src:12189-12193)
GIVEN `the determination is that it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trials are being held in different territorial divisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the content` IS A `s 551.7(3) the content of the order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551.7(3) the Chief Justice or Chief Judge shall issue an order with the content` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the determination is that it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge or his or her designate determines that it is in the interests of justice to adjudicate the issue at a joint hearing"
        IF `the content` EQUALS `s 551.7(3) anything else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "he or she shall issue an order (a) declaring that a joint hearing be held"
        IF `the content` EQUALS `s 551.7(3)(d) designating the territorial division in which the hearing is to be held` AND NOT `the trials are being held in different territorial divisions` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trials are being held in different territorial divisions"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 551.7 (4) However, the order may only be made in respect of a trial for an indictable offence, other than a trial before a provincial court judge, if the indictment has been preferred.
